  "pressure": {
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "p1",
     "type": "image",
     "x": 6,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 6,
     "h": 10,
     "caption": "Image",
     "src": "/uploads/20261009-md1d1txo.jpg"
    },
    {
     "id": "p2",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 6,
     "h": 10,
     "size": "m",
     "html": "<div><div><div><div><div><div><span><div>This project rethinks architecture as a climate-controlled open-air environment, where circulation becomes the primary program. Utilizing earth tubes as a passive thermal regulating system, spaces remain open yet moderated.</div></span></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div><div><div><div><span><div><span><br>Our project features a continuous running track wrapping around the exterior of the building, organizing it as a vertical landscape rather than a stack of floors. Going from the ground to the top and back down is a little over a mile.<br><br>The ground floor features two changing rooms, a six lane pool as well as the entrance to the running track. <br><br>As the user moves along the track, the space is experienced through changes in light, exposure and elevation, simulating the experiences of trail running.<br><br>Below, the underground introduces a contrasting condition, being mostly enclosed, almost cave like. Housing programs such as server rooms and sauna rooms. <br><br>Together, the project establishes a vertical sequence of atmospheres, shifting from exposure above to containment below.<br><br>Ultimately, our project reframes architecture as a continuous environmental and spatial experience, shaped by climate, movement and time</span></div></span></div></div></div></div></div>"
    },
